 only going to last you  roughly hour and a half or so if you're  really pushing the machine so what do we  learned from all this testing well you  definitely get diminishing returns  getting extra graphics course from 14 to  16 most cases it's not worth it unless  you need the cpu performance and for  most video editing tasks you won't  really see that same thing goes from the  24 to 32 core  you're not going to get that much better  performance unless you're gaming which  not very many people are or you're doing  something like noise reduction and still  the difference isn't that big but it's  going to run hotter the battery life is  definitely worse on the 32 core and if  you're really pushing the machine it  could actually perform worse  than the cheaper 24 core model so the 24  core with mmo max is the bang for the  buck it is the sweet spot it is really  really well optimized for that chassis  and  if you want to save a little money get  the base one that one runs really cool  really quiet and it has insane battery  life only dropping 20 percent after 45  minutes of heavy heavy  use so my suggestion  if you can get a 16 inch you can deal  with it go for it better battery life  you get great performance and it  literally  the 16 inch 2500 one had the same  performance as a specked out 14 inch  which is just it's crazy so there you  guys go the full comparison between all  of the graphics options that you can get  let me know your thoughts down below  click that circle above if you guys want  to subscribe and help us reach our goal  of 1 million subscribers check out one  of those great videos right over there  this has been max and i will see you in  the next video  [Music]
 

